WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.790 --> 00:00:07.640
“In the autumn of 1918, as the empire for
which they had fought was collapsing around

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:12.889
them, weary soldiers of the Habsburg imperial
and royal army made their way back to their

00:00:12.889 --> 00:00:13.889
homelands.

00:00:13.889 --> 00:00:18.270
For some of the higher Habsburg officers,
however, the dissolution of the old Austro-Hungarian

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:20.750
empire created a unique dilemma.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:26.320
Some of them had spent so many years as servants
of the emperor, and had grown so accustomed

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:31.610
to the international flavor of the Habsburg
military life, that they found it difficult

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:36.580
to switch their loyalty to any of the new
nation states that were arising from the ruins

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:41.840
of the old empire … In the days after the
armistice, these disoriented men, for whom

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:47.850
the future seemed particularly bleak and uncharted,
gravitated to Vienna, there to pay their final

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:53.680
tribute to Karl, the last reigning ruler of
the six hundred year old dynasty.”

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:58.720
One of these men, who appeared in Vienna for
his last audience with the emperor was none

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:04.580
other than the Rear-Admiral Miklos Horthy,
the Commander in Chief of the Habsburg Navy.

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:09.560
During his last audience with the Emperor,
Miklos Horthy, trembling and with tears in

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:14.530
his eyes, vowed that “I will never rest
until I have restored your Majesty to his

00:01:14.530 --> 00:01:16.980
throne in Vienna and Budapest”.

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:23.080
Who, however, was this 50 year old admiral
called Miklos Horthy, where did he come from,

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:26.210
and did he eventually fulfill his promise
to the emperor?

00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:27.770
Well, let's find out.

00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:28.780
But before we do.

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:33.060
This video is part of a greater Historytuber
collaboration called Project Dictator where

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:37.660
multiple historytubers talk about the history
behind various people that have been called

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:40.940
dictators, or tyrants or similar in the past.

00:01:40.940 --> 00:01:45.189
If you want to see all those videos head on
to the Project Dictator playlist, link in

00:01:45.189 --> 00:01:47.920
the top right corner, description and pinned
comment.

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:50.560
Biography of Miklós Horthy

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:57.189
Miklos Horthy was born in 1868 to low nobility
in the Hungarian town of Kenderes.

00:01:57.189 --> 00:02:02.730
His father was a member of the Hungarian parliament,
and, overall, his family, even though low

00:02:02.730 --> 00:02:08.459
nobility, wasn’t poor by any means and controlled
around a 610 hectare estate.

00:02:08.459 --> 00:02:14.040
Miklos Horthy was not neglected by his parents
but he was one of 8 children and in such an

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:17.629
environment his parents’ attention was often
divided.

00:02:17.629 --> 00:02:22.739
This, combined with Horthy’s “desire for
adventure”, meant that at his own behest,

00:02:22.739 --> 00:02:27.989
Horthy was sent to multiple boarding schools
first in Debrecen and later in Sopron.

00:02:27.989 --> 00:02:33.129
When Horthy was 14, his older brother was
accidentally killed during a naval exercise

00:02:33.129 --> 00:02:38.650
in the Royal Naval Academy, after this unfortunate
accident, Horthy decided that he wanted to

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:42.900
follow in his late brother's footsteps, and
enrolled in the "Imperial and Royal Naval

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:45.099
Academy" in today’s Rijeka.

00:02:45.099 --> 00:02:50.730
Here, just like in his previous schools at
Debrecen and Sopron, Horthy showed average

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:54.620
ability in almost all his subjects but one,
languages.

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:59.959
He seemed to have a knack for learning new
languages and quickly, on top of already knowing

00:02:59.959 --> 00:03:04.540
French, German and Hungarian, picked up full
fluency in Italian, and Croatian.

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:09.449
Once he graduated, and officially joined the
Navy, Horthy would also learn a sundry of

00:03:09.449 --> 00:03:14.159
other languages most notably English which
he learned while stationed in Pola.

00:03:14.159 --> 00:03:20.650
His English teacher in Pola was, at the time,
an unknown poor writer called James Joyce.

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:25.599
While stationed in Pola Horthy also learned
how to sing and play the piano thanks in part

00:03:25.599 --> 00:03:29.040
to the local Royal Navy band leader, Franz
Lehar.

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:34.430
Horthy seemed quite content with his place
in the navy and very much enjoyed the opportunities

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:39.390
the navy provided, especially the ability
to see the world and meet new people.

00:03:39.390 --> 00:03:45.799
He traveled as a naval liaison to far flung
places like the Ottoman Empire, New Zealand,

00:03:45.799 --> 00:03:48.809
India, Borneo, Portugal, England, etc.

00:03:48.809 --> 00:03:53.989
Everywhere he went he was always enthusiastically
welcomed by the local high society not only

00:03:53.989 --> 00:03:59.239
because of his language and conversation skills,
and his reputation as a perfect victorian

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:03.489
gentleman, but also because of his dancing,
music, and athletic skills.

00:04:03.489 --> 00:04:07.180
He was an avid fencer, equestrian, and a tennis
player.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:12.159
During his travels Horthy also developed great
admiration for the British Royal Navy stating

00:04:12.159 --> 00:04:16.880
“the proud saying … ‘Britannia rules
the waves’ prevailed; we have seen many

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:19.790
profound examples of this throughout our journey.”

00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:24.790
Due to Horthy’s experiences abroad, his
excellent language and social skills, and,

00:04:24.790 --> 00:04:29.510
his competence when it came to actual naval
command, he steadily climbed up the carrier

00:04:29.510 --> 00:04:31.470
poll in the Royal Navy.

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:37.130
Most notably becoming the naval advisor to
the Emperor Franz Joseph in 1909 at the age

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:38.380
of 41.

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:44.040
It was here, in Vienna, where Horthy was introduced
to the inner workings of the Empire and formulated

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:47.560
many of his conservative monarchist political
ideas.

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:52.450
Vienna during that time was apparently the
place to be as not just Horthy and Franz Joseph

00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:57.900
lived in Vienna but also Hitler, Tito, Stalin,
Trotsky, Freud, and many others.

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:00.200
If you want to know more, I made a video about
it.

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:06.680
When the Great War started, Horthy, now 46,
was a commander of SMS Habsburg, but this

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:08.260
was only the beginning.

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:12.631
One historian described Horthy’s rise through
the ranks during the 4 year period of the

00:05:12.631 --> 00:05:14.880
Great War as “meteoric”.

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:20.730
He proved his naval skills early on during
several naval encounters in the Adriatic sea,

00:05:20.730 --> 00:05:26.630
and on top of being given a myriad of Austro-Hungarian
military awards, he was even awarded the German

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:32.890
Iron Cross both first and, second class, in
1915, due to his successful efforts of escorting

00:05:32.890 --> 00:05:35.810
German U-Boats through an entente blockade.

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:42.500
In 1917 he planned, led, and successfully
executed an entire operation which resulted

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:47.830
in the largest WW1 naval battle in the Adriatic
sea, the Battle of the Otranto Strait.

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:53.190
During the battle Horthy was outnumbered and
wounded, but continued to issue orders for

00:05:53.190 --> 00:05:56.680
hours until he eventually collapsed from blood
loss.

00:05:56.680 --> 00:06:01.140
He was praised all throughout the Empire as
a war hero, especially by Hungarians who viewed

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:04.120
him as the most notable Magyar of the Great
War.

00:06:04.120 --> 00:06:09.460
Due to all this Horthy was appointed as the
Commander in Chief of the Habsburg navy in

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:10.460
1918.

00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:16.030
This new command would not last long as sadly
for Horthy, the war ended with the breaking

00:06:16.030 --> 00:06:19.560
up of the Empire into a myriad of national
components.

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:24.460
Horthy would later recall that surrendering
the Habsburg Navy to the entente, along with

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:28.550
all the other events that occurred in central
Europe after the war, were one of the saddest

00:06:28.550 --> 00:06:29.980
moments of his life.

00:06:29.980 --> 00:06:35.030
The empire he served his entire life was destroyed
and the country which he was supposed to call

00:06:35.030 --> 00:06:39.610
home was beset by enemies on all sides ready
to divide its territory.

00:06:39.610 --> 00:06:44.990
Horthy, however, was not a politician and
after his last meeting with the emperor returned

00:06:44.990 --> 00:06:50.810
to his family estate in Kenderes where, as
Thomas Sakmyster puts it, “He no doubt hoped

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:56.830
to spend his remaining years as a country
squire far removed from the political machinations

00:06:56.830 --> 00:06:58.870
of Budapest and Vienna.”

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:00.770
But fate had other plans.

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:06.440
In early 1919, the Hungarian government resigned
in protest against the entente demands.

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:11.070
The ensuing power vacuum was exploited by
the Hungarian communists who seized power

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:13.660
and established the Hungarian Soviet Republic.

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:19.139
With the rise of Hungarian communism Horthy
suddenly became directly affected by the politics

00:07:19.139 --> 00:07:20.139
he hoped to avoid.

00:07:20.139 --> 00:07:24.404
Biography of Miklós Horthy : The Fellowship
of the Counter-Revolution

00:07:24.404 --> 00:07:29.870
The establishment of the Hungarian Soviet
Republic was, for Horthy, like a bad dream.

00:07:29.870 --> 00:07:35.180
He, and many of his fellow landholders of
the old aristocracy, suddenly became targets

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:40.139
of the communist government and his brother
was even briefly imprisoned in Budapest.

00:07:40.139 --> 00:07:44.780
The peasants in the Kenderes area were on
multiple occasions urged by the communists

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:49.889
arriving from Budapest to seize the estates
and manor houses of the local nobility and

00:07:49.889 --> 00:07:53.860
rise up against their oppressors including
Horthy and his family.

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:58.139
We do not have any details of what exactly
might have happened in Kenderes during this

00:07:58.139 --> 00:08:03.050
time or how much was Horthy and his family
affected by some radicalized peasants swept

00:08:03.050 --> 00:08:04.880
up in the communist fervor.

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:09.860
However, it is safe to assume that some confrontations
between the peasants and the landowners did

00:08:09.860 --> 00:08:11.900
occur during this time in Kenderes.

00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:17.740
The rise of the Hungarian Soviet Republic
also brought about a rise in targeted executions

00:08:17.740 --> 00:08:22.300
and acts of terorrism against people deemed
as enemies of communism.

00:08:22.300 --> 00:08:26.980
These killings and terrorist acts became to
be known in Hungary as the Red Terror.

00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:31.230
The antagonism of his own peasants combined
with the red terror sweeping across the country

00:08:31.230 --> 00:08:35.300
made Horthy despise the communists and everything
they stood for.

00:08:35.300 --> 00:08:40.050
It was also at this time that Horthy, along
with many other counterrevolutionaries, came

00:08:40.050 --> 00:08:45.680
to formulate quite strong antisemetic ideas
mostly spurred on by the fact that a lot of

00:08:45.680 --> 00:08:49.160
the Hungarian communists happened to be of
jewish origin.

00:08:49.160 --> 00:08:55.290
For example, the leader of the Soviet Republic,
Bela Kun, and 20 of his 26 commissars, were

00:08:55.290 --> 00:08:56.660
all of jewish origin.

00:08:56.660 --> 00:09:01.850
The exact reasons for this fairly large involvement
of jews in the Hungarian Soviet Republic are

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:06.670
still being debated by historians today but
it is prudent to mention that numbers wise

00:09:06.670 --> 00:09:12.059
jews were still a minority and most Hungarian
communists were ethnic Hungarians.

00:09:12.059 --> 00:09:17.610
Nonetheless, Horthy, as a believer in old
Habsburg monarchist ideas, viewed Bela Kun,

00:09:17.610 --> 00:09:22.790
and his quote “jewish” Soviet Republic,
as the most dangerous movement ready to destroy

00:09:22.790 --> 00:09:24.779
the Hungarian way of life.

00:09:24.779 --> 00:09:30.240
For Horthy, Kun, and his government, was even
more dangerous to Hungary than the neighboring

00:09:30.240 --> 00:09:33.249
countries taking over Hungarian land.

00:09:33.249 --> 00:09:39.740
So, when, in the spring of 1919, Horthy, the
most notable Hungarian war hero, received

00:09:39.740 --> 00:09:44.829
a letter from a counterrevolutionary government
forming in Szeged if he wanted the command

00:09:44.829 --> 00:09:47.290
of the newly created “National Army”.

00:09:47.290 --> 00:09:52.300
Horthy, wanting to put an end to the Hungarian
Soviet Republic and maybe reconquer back some

00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:58.029
of the lost Hungarian lands, enthusiastically
accepted this offer and arrived in Szeged

00:09:58.029 --> 00:10:00.620
30 of May 1919.

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:05.410
During his first cabinet meeting of the counter
revolutionary government Horthy proclaimed

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:09.959
“I couldn’t sit in Kenderes listening
to the grass rustling in the wind, when my

00:10:09.959 --> 00:10:12.680
poor fatherland lise in ruins.

00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:16.120
It has been a difficult inner conflict, but
I have come.

00:10:16.120 --> 00:10:17.699
I accept the responsibility.

00:10:17.699 --> 00:10:20.420
I am at your command.”

00:10:20.420 --> 00:10:25.430
Horthy’s first and only task was to form,
organize, and train the “National Army”.

00:10:25.430 --> 00:10:30.199
This, unsurprisingly, proved to be a very
difficult task with mixed results.

00:10:30.199 --> 00:10:34.920
Due to the ongoing wars between the Hungarian
Soviet Republic, Czechoslovakia, and Romania,

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:38.200
Horthy could only muster up men from the local
area.

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:42.920
For more context on the history of post war
Hungary watch my Dissolution of Hungary video.

00:10:42.920 --> 00:10:48.879
As a result of these circumstances, by July,
Horthy had only around 5k men.

00:10:48.879 --> 00:10:53.610
However, despite these small numbers, Horthy’s
story started to circulate throughout the

00:10:53.610 --> 00:10:54.869
entire country.

00:10:54.869 --> 00:10:59.600
This story presented a man, a leader, who
would often entertain the men in the pub by

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:05.041
singing and playing the piano, by sharing
anecdotes of far flung lands he visited, by

00:11:05.041 --> 00:11:08.269
telling war stories of maritime adventures.

00:11:08.269 --> 00:11:13.959
Here was a war hero, an aristocrat of the
old regime who, to the common soldiers, seemed

00:11:13.959 --> 00:11:15.250
like one of them.

00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:20.149
It did not matter, even to the most fervent
nationalists, that Horthy’s Hungarian was

00:11:20.149 --> 00:11:26.430
quote “simple”, spoken with a German accent,
and often intermixed with German or even English

00:11:26.430 --> 00:11:30.350
words and phrases when Hungarian ones didn’t
come to mind.

00:11:30.350 --> 00:11:36.279
That merely added to the international character
of this national hero who clearly spent a

00:11:36.279 --> 00:11:42.160
long time away from Hungary but has now come
home to liberate it, to raise it to greatness.

00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:47.400
These early post-war months were the very
beginnings of what came to be Horthy’s leader

00:11:47.400 --> 00:11:48.400
cult.

00:11:48.400 --> 00:11:51.380
However, not all Hungarians saw in him a hero.

00:11:51.380 --> 00:11:56.839
Many workers living in larger cities viewed
Horthy as an old aristocrat who was content

00:11:56.839 --> 00:12:02.930
with the status quo and, therefore, will bring
no change, no glory, and no prosperity to

00:12:02.930 --> 00:12:04.610
the struggling country.

00:12:04.610 --> 00:12:08.809
When it came to the politicians of the counter
revolutionary government who invited Horthy

00:12:08.809 --> 00:12:10.260
to lead the army.

00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:15.110
They saw in him nothing more than a military
figurehead whose popularity could be used

00:12:15.110 --> 00:12:18.259
to form an army and establish a new government.

00:12:18.259 --> 00:12:23.339
They certainly did not expect Horthy to meddle
in the political side of the counterrevolution

00:12:23.339 --> 00:12:25.160
and initially they were right.

00:12:25.160 --> 00:12:30.199
Horthy seemed to have been very apathetic
towards politics and often just quietly did

00:12:30.199 --> 00:12:33.300
his duties as the commander of the national
army.

00:12:33.300 --> 00:12:40.459
This national army, during the summer of 1919,
began to attract ever more radicalized right-wing

00:12:40.459 --> 00:12:41.459
extremists.

00:12:41.459 --> 00:12:46.360
Many of the men joining the army were Hungarians
driven from their homes by either Hungarian

00:12:46.360 --> 00:12:51.369
Communists or hostile governments of Czechoslovakia,
Romania and Yugoslavia.

00:12:51.369 --> 00:12:57.649
These men underwent the “radicalizing effects
of the refugee experience” and held fierce

00:12:57.649 --> 00:13:02.550
nationalistic, anti-semetic, anticommunist,
militaristic, and iridentist ideas.

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:07.449
The most prominent of these right-wing extremists
were within the officer core.

00:13:07.449 --> 00:13:11.360
People like Gombos, Kozma, Ostenburg, Pronay,
etc.

00:13:11.360 --> 00:13:15.929
These people were also the ones that spent
the most time with Horthy as his army advisors

00:13:15.929 --> 00:13:20.959
and, therefore, could stoke within him ever
more radical right-wing beliefs.

00:13:20.959 --> 00:13:26.959
Horthy wasn’t opposed to this and, as stated
before, he already fostered his own antisemetic,

00:13:26.959 --> 00:13:32.089
anticommunist, and irredentist feelings, but
it was in Szeged where he began to be far

00:13:32.089 --> 00:13:33.970
more radicalized then before.

00:13:33.970 --> 00:13:38.920
In his own words “I am now capable of anything
… if necessary, I’ll use strychnine poison

00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:41.279
and employ the basest methods.

00:13:41.279 --> 00:13:45.399
After all, our enemies have treated us like
corpses to be desecrated.”

00:13:45.399 --> 00:13:50.750
Since Horthy had become quite radicalized
at this point it was not unsurprising that,

00:13:50.750 --> 00:13:56.709
when his officers like Pronay started to assassinate
political opponents and jews in and around

00:13:56.709 --> 00:14:00.119
Szeged, he turned a blind eye to all these
killings.

00:14:00.119 --> 00:14:04.529
Even when the politicians in the counter revolutionary
government started to pressure Horthy to stop

00:14:04.529 --> 00:14:06.439
the killings, Horthy did nothing.

00:14:06.439 --> 00:14:11.499
In fact, he even praised Pronay and appointed
him as his personal bodyguard.

00:14:11.499 --> 00:14:17.749
Then, in August of 1919, the Hungarian Soviet
republic fell to the Romanian advance and

00:14:17.749 --> 00:14:20.589
the counter revolutionary government sprung
into action.

00:14:20.589 --> 00:14:24.970
The National Army numbers started to steadily
rise and the counter revolutionary government

00:14:24.970 --> 00:14:30.329
quickly sent out parts of this growing national
army to western Hungary in order to take control

00:14:30.329 --> 00:14:31.329
of it.

00:14:31.329 --> 00:14:35.429
The leaders of this expedition were the radical
right-wing officers like Pronay and Mikos

00:14:35.429 --> 00:14:41.889
Kozma who stated that “Both the red and
the pink eras are over … Those who for months

00:14:41.889 --> 00:14:45.569
have committed heinous crimes must receive
their punishment.

00:14:45.569 --> 00:14:50.459
It is predictable … that the compromisers
and those with weak stomachs will moan and

00:14:50.459 --> 00:14:55.269
groan when we line up a few red rogouse and
terrorists against the walls.

00:14:55.269 --> 00:15:00.230
Once before the false slogans of humanism
and other ‘isms’ helped drive the country

00:15:00.230 --> 00:15:01.499
into ruin.

00:15:01.499 --> 00:15:04.110
This second time they will wail in vain.”

00:15:04.110 --> 00:15:09.110
Horthy’s orders to the departing officers
were only given verbally and there’s no

00:15:09.110 --> 00:15:12.389
record surviving that could tell us what those
orders were.

00:15:12.389 --> 00:15:16.889
However, it is almost certain that Horthy
knew the intentions of his officers and that

00:15:16.889 --> 00:15:20.019
he himself chose to send these specific men.

00:15:20.019 --> 00:15:24.670
He was more than aware of what these radicalized
men were planning to do and we have to assume

00:15:24.670 --> 00:15:28.529
that’s what he wanted as in the end he was
the one who sent them.

00:15:28.529 --> 00:15:34.379
There is even a quote surviving from Horthy’s
chief of staff Karoly Soos who told Pronay

00:15:34.379 --> 00:15:40.410
before leaving “Don’t kill too many jews,
since that will create problems too.”

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:45.389
With their orders in hand and their minds
made up the radical right-wing officers of

00:15:45.389 --> 00:15:51.269
the national army went on a campaign of what
they called “purification” in mostly western

00:15:51.269 --> 00:15:52.269
hungary.

00:15:52.269 --> 00:15:57.310
The majority of the national army, mostly
the lower rank consrcipts, did not take part

00:15:57.310 --> 00:16:02.220
in the heinous crimes and killings of jews
and people who were suspected of having communist

00:16:02.220 --> 00:16:07.579
sympathies even when there was no proof; but
a substantial number of the officer core of

00:16:07.579 --> 00:16:12.360
the army did conduct these crimes which became
to be called the White Terror.

00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:17.579
As Horthy was working on retaking Budapest
from the Romanian occupation, newspapers started

00:16:17.579 --> 00:16:21.799
to publish the stories of the white terror
happening all accross western Hungary.

00:16:21.799 --> 00:16:26.850
When these reports reached Horthy and the
people around him he did nothing and simply

00:16:26.850 --> 00:16:28.899
just dismissed the news.

00:16:28.899 --> 00:16:33.620
Then when Pronay returned to Horthy, Horthy
told him to “continue the excellent job

00:16:33.620 --> 00:16:35.239
he has been doing”.

00:16:35.239 --> 00:16:40.049
Even when Hungarian politicians and entente
ambassadors started to put ever more pressure

00:16:40.049 --> 00:16:44.970
on Horthy to stop the White terror Horthy
still remained silent on the whole issue.

00:16:44.970 --> 00:16:49.379
Hearing out the concerns of the politicians
and the entente ambassadors but not doing

00:16:49.379 --> 00:16:50.749
anything about it.

00:16:50.749 --> 00:16:56.380
There is no evidence to prove or disprove
that Horthy ever directly ordered or participated

00:16:56.380 --> 00:17:01.500
in any of the executions of the White Terror
but he certainly intially did not stop it,

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:06.050
or even tryed to stop it, despite clearly
being aware of it happening.

00:17:06.050 --> 00:17:10.140
Meanwhile the political situation in Hungary
had gotten complicated.

00:17:10.140 --> 00:17:14.709
The Szeged government disbanded, a new counter
revolutionary government was founded in Budapest

00:17:14.709 --> 00:17:19.380
after the communists fled, another counter
revolutionary government was coming from Vienna,

00:17:19.380 --> 00:17:23.560
and “there were multiple local governments
and strongmen who exerted control across the

00:17:23.560 --> 00:17:25.339
occupied lands of Hungary.”

00:17:25.339 --> 00:17:30.500
When the Szeged government fell apart Horthy
found himself at the head of an ever growing

00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:33.400
National Army which was now without a government.

00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:37.770
Despite this, Horthy continued on as normal
as if nothing happened and was getting his

00:17:37.770 --> 00:17:42.690
national army ready to retake Budapest after
the Romanians were ordered by the entente

00:17:42.690 --> 00:17:43.690
to withdraw.

00:17:43.690 --> 00:17:48.530
This caused a lot of concern for many Hungarian
politicians from the various counter revolutionary

00:17:48.530 --> 00:17:49.550
governments.

00:17:49.550 --> 00:17:55.510
After all Budapest was the city which enthusiastically
supported the communists, still had many communist

00:17:55.510 --> 00:17:58.640
sympathizers, and had a large jewish population.

00:17:58.640 --> 00:18:03.620
Therefore, many politicians were afraid of
what the National Army could do in Budapest

00:18:03.620 --> 00:18:06.440
considering what they were doing in the countryside.

00:18:06.440 --> 00:18:11.570
In order to try to prevent any mass killings
to happen in Budapest a group of senior Hungarian

00:18:11.570 --> 00:18:15.790
statesmen organized a meeting with Horthy
to try to plead with him.

00:18:15.790 --> 00:18:20.780
During the meeting, at the end of a fairly
distressing conversation in which Horthy seemed

00:18:20.780 --> 00:18:26.040
to have continuously refuse to address the
main issue, one of the statesmen finally lost

00:18:26.040 --> 00:18:32.050
his temper and asked plainly “If the national
army enters the capital city, will there be

00:18:32.050 --> 00:18:38.350
a pogrom - YES or NO?” to which Horthy replied
“There will be no pogrom, but a few people

00:18:38.350 --> 00:18:40.420
will have to take a swim.”

00:18:40.420 --> 00:18:46.210
Despite Horthy’s not completely satisfactory
answer the meeting ended on a positive note

00:18:46.210 --> 00:18:51.080
as the Hungarian statesmen were happy to hear
Horthy say “there will be no pogrom”.

00:18:51.080 --> 00:18:56.310
The meeting was also a start to a series of
events which slowly lead Horthy away from

00:18:56.310 --> 00:18:59.070
the thinking of his radical right-wing officers.

00:18:59.070 --> 00:19:03.630
The fact that some of the most senior Hungarian
politicians were afraid of what Horthy’s

00:19:03.630 --> 00:19:08.780
army was doing started to open Horthy’s
eyes to the idea that perhaps the White Terror

00:19:08.780 --> 00:19:10.010
has gone too far.

00:19:10.010 --> 00:19:14.700
He even met with the representatives of the
Jewish community of Budapest to hear their

00:19:14.700 --> 00:19:17.720
side of the story before his takeover of the
city.

00:19:17.720 --> 00:19:24.240
By the end of 1919 Horthy still did not completely
denounce the work of his officers and outside

00:19:24.240 --> 00:19:29.790
of few pardons which he gave to several jews
and communists captured by his army he still

00:19:29.790 --> 00:19:34.800
remained in silent support of the White Terror,
but over all he did start a clear slow shift

00:19:34.800 --> 00:19:38.490
away from the radical right-wing ideas and
their proponents.

00:19:38.490 --> 00:19:44.410
With that said, despite this “softening”
of Horthy, Gombos and other right winged officers

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:49.880
still saw Horthy as a strong leader and the
best bet for establishing an authoritative

00:19:49.880 --> 00:19:51.420
nationalistic state.

00:19:51.420 --> 00:19:56.550
Therefore, they started to organize a large
propaganda campaign, mostly headed by Gombos,

00:19:56.550 --> 00:20:01.410
to expand the leader cult around Horthy and
to promote him as the only viable leader who

00:20:01.410 --> 00:20:02.710
can save Hungary.

00:20:02.710 --> 00:20:07.720
Horthy didn’t order this propaganda campaign
but he also didn’t stop it and probably

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:12.270
at the very least felt flattered that his
officers organized it.

00:20:12.270 --> 00:20:18.030
The National Army marched into Budapest, with
Horthy leading it atop a white horse, 16th

00:20:18.030 --> 00:20:20.030
of November 1919.

00:20:20.030 --> 00:20:25.510
The pogrom in Budapest that so many were fearing
did not happen as Horthy gave clear instructions

00:20:25.510 --> 00:20:29.610
to not repeat in Budapest that what happened
in rural Hungary.

00:20:29.610 --> 00:20:34.260
After taking Budapest Horthy was advised by
many of his radical right-wing officers to

00:20:34.260 --> 00:20:39.210
establish a military dictatorship and conquer
back the lost lands of Hungary.

00:20:39.210 --> 00:20:44.110
After all, at this point he was the only man
in Hungary with an army and now even had the

00:20:44.110 --> 00:20:46.240
capital city in his control.

00:20:46.240 --> 00:20:48.500
Horthy, however, did not do this.

00:20:48.500 --> 00:20:50.880
The reasons for why were multiple.

00:20:50.880 --> 00:20:56.790
First, Horthy still saw himself as a military
man, a person who shouldn’t play a significant

00:20:56.790 --> 00:21:02.570
part in politics and a person who should always
be loyal to his king who, at this point, still

00:21:02.570 --> 00:21:05.050
had a chance of returning to Hungary.

00:21:05.050 --> 00:21:10.230
Second, there was almost no chance that the
entente would tolerate an irredentist military

00:21:10.230 --> 00:21:14.950
dictatorship in Hungary, especially not after
what happened with the communists.

00:21:14.950 --> 00:21:19.560
Therefore, Horthy continued to play the part
of an apolitical military leader who would

00:21:19.560 --> 00:21:22.400
support the establishment of a coalition government.

00:21:22.400 --> 00:21:26.830
With that said, while playing this part of
an apolitical military leader, Horthy did

00:21:26.830 --> 00:21:33.210
slowly increase his involvement in politics,
from 1919 to 1920, but largely only in support

00:21:33.210 --> 00:21:37.800
of other politicians he agreed with rather
than as an independent figure.

00:21:37.800 --> 00:21:42.780
With the capital now back in Hungarian control
the entente set about establishing a coalition

00:21:42.780 --> 00:21:47.140
government combining all the various independent
counterrevolutionary administrations that

00:21:47.140 --> 00:21:48.770
sprang up all around Hungary.

00:21:48.770 --> 00:21:54.000
This coalition government was to oversee an
election held in January of 1920.

00:21:54.000 --> 00:21:59.430
The election was boycotted by the social democrats
in respons to the oppressive actions against

00:21:59.430 --> 00:22:03.610
leftist parties during the White Terror which
still continued in the coutry side.

00:22:03.610 --> 00:22:08.330
Due to this, and the overall counter revolutionary
sentiment that spread across Hungary after

00:22:08.330 --> 00:22:13.380
the fall of the Hungarian Soviet Republic,
the government which was elected was overwhelmingly

00:22:13.380 --> 00:22:16.870
conservative and in favor of restoring the
monarchy.

00:22:16.870 --> 00:22:22.600
The entente, however, at this point made it
very clear that they will not tolerate any

00:22:22.600 --> 00:22:25.260
return of Habsburg rule in Hungary.

00:22:25.260 --> 00:22:30.790
This meant that the overwhelmingly monarchist
government had to look for a different solution.

00:22:30.790 --> 00:22:36.160
This different solution came in the form of
electing a regent who “could preside over

00:22:36.160 --> 00:22:41.770
the recovery of his country and hold the reins
of power until conditions were more propitious

00:22:41.770 --> 00:22:43.960
for Karl von Hasburg’s return.”

00:22:43.960 --> 00:22:48.900
As for who would fill this position of a regent
there was really no question.

00:22:48.900 --> 00:22:53.280
Sure there were more senior and higher ranking
nobles in Hungary who could be elected as

00:22:53.280 --> 00:22:58.430
regents but Horthy’s popularity among the
people at this point was unmatched by any

00:22:58.430 --> 00:22:59.950
other Hungarian.

00:22:59.950 --> 00:23:04.450
Despite his hand in the White Terror he seemed
to have publicly distance himself enough from

00:23:04.450 --> 00:23:09.690
it, while still not actively stopping it,
that by 1920 many people viewed Horthy as

00:23:09.690 --> 00:23:13.130
the most viable candidate despite his chequered
past.

00:23:13.130 --> 00:23:17.460
Not to mention that his radical right-wing
officers were still actively working on a

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:22.310
propaganda campaign around his leader cult
hoping that Horthy would eventually establish

00:23:22.310 --> 00:23:24.880
that desired military dictatorship.

00:23:24.880 --> 00:23:28.980
When it came to the politicians themselves,
some had gripes with Horthy.

00:23:28.980 --> 00:23:34.620
Such as his poor skill of the Hungarian language
which was allegedly just as bad as the Hungarian

00:23:34.620 --> 00:23:40.480
of Franz Joseph, or his poor understanding
of statecraft and politics, but, for the most

00:23:40.480 --> 00:23:44.740
part, many still viewed Horthy as a man who
could be controlled and didn’t have large

00:23:44.740 --> 00:23:46.630
aspirations for power.

00:23:46.630 --> 00:23:51.220
After all he had an opportunity to establish
a military dictatorship when he took Budapest

00:23:51.220 --> 00:23:52.280
but he didn’t.

00:23:52.280 --> 00:23:57.680
So, when it came to the Parliamentary vote
to choose a regent, Horthy was elected in

00:23:57.680 --> 00:23:59.130
a landslide (95%).

00:23:59.130 --> 00:24:03.580
He, however, did something which many of the
politicians did not expect.

00:24:03.580 --> 00:24:08.870
He refused to take the regency, stating that
he cannot accept a position which was gutted

00:24:08.870 --> 00:24:14.100
of its function by parliament and demanded
to have more power as regent, such as the

00:24:14.100 --> 00:24:16.150
ability to dissolve parliament.

00:24:16.150 --> 00:24:21.370
The parliament was furious, but they also
couldn’t realistically deny Horthy’s request

00:24:21.370 --> 00:24:26.600
as they did just elect him in an overwhelming
majority and Horthy’s loyal army officers

00:24:26.600 --> 00:24:29.810
were currently stationed in Budapest just
in case.

00:24:29.810 --> 00:24:33.950
Whether Horthy actually planned to have the
army officers stationed in Budapest as an

00:24:33.950 --> 00:24:38.710
intimidation tactic or the officers were acting
of their own accord is hard to say.

00:24:38.710 --> 00:24:45.710
In any case, parliament acquiesced to Horthy’s
demands who subsequently, on March 1st 1920,

00:24:45.710 --> 00:24:50.620
swore an oath to protect the Hungarian people
and nation as its regent.

00:24:50.620 --> 00:24:56.010
Now as the regent, with increased political
power, Horthy could no longer play the card

00:24:56.010 --> 00:24:58.010
of silence and indifference.

00:24:58.010 --> 00:25:01.320
He had to choose sides or risk losing his
position.

00:25:01.320 --> 00:25:06.760
Therefore, harkening back to his old deeply
entrenched monarchist roots, Horthy sided

00:25:06.760 --> 00:25:11.530
with the so-called “old conservatives”,
the monarchists of the parliament, and his

00:25:11.530 --> 00:25:16.380
days of silently supporting the radical right-wing
army officers and politicians were coming

00:25:16.380 --> 00:25:17.380
to an end.

00:25:17.380 --> 00:25:22.580
This wasn’t an overnight change and it did
take more than a year to manifest but by the

00:25:22.580 --> 00:25:28.740
end 1921 the White Terror finaly ended as
Horthy withdrew his silent support and even

00:25:28.740 --> 00:25:31.160
enacted certain laws that would stop it.

00:25:31.160 --> 00:25:36.170
The exact numbers of the White Terror are
impossible to determin as no real records

00:25:36.170 --> 00:25:39.880
where kept by the perpetrators but definitely
at least 1000 (with some historians stating

00:25:39.880 --> 00:25:43.370
more than 5000) people lost their lives with
tens of thousands (around 70,000) injured

00:25:43.370 --> 00:25:44.810
maimed and imprisoned.

00:25:44.810 --> 00:25:49.420
Horthy finally detached himself from the radical
right-wing officers and politicians and started

00:25:49.420 --> 00:25:53.020
to even support some jewish and socialist
programs.

00:25:53.020 --> 00:25:57.870
Like the governmental financial recovery plan
funded by jewish capital, or the allowing

00:25:57.870 --> 00:26:02.310
of leftist parties to print their newspapers
which they where forced to stop during the

00:26:02.310 --> 00:26:03.520
White Terror.

00:26:03.520 --> 00:26:09.050
Horthy still retained some antisemtic prejudice
but no longer was he going to support active

00:26:09.050 --> 00:26:11.400
eradication and suppression of them.

00:26:11.400 --> 00:26:15.770
When it came to communism, Horthy also retained
a strong anti-communist sentiment for pretty

00:26:15.770 --> 00:26:20.620
much his entire life, but again he was also
no longer going to support active killing

00:26:20.620 --> 00:26:22.480
of communists in Hungary.

00:26:22.480 --> 00:26:27.840
Horthy’s former radical right-wing friends
were furious with him, accusing him of becoming

00:26:27.840 --> 00:26:33.130
“soft” a “jew loving aristocrat” a
“drugged puppet” of the “freemasons”,

00:26:33.130 --> 00:26:36.060
they basically became the YouTube comments.

00:26:36.060 --> 00:26:41.690
In 1923, in opposition to the old conservatives,
these right-wing radicals formed their own

00:26:41.690 --> 00:26:46.950
party called the Racial Defense which from
its name you can probably guess what it was

00:26:46.950 --> 00:26:47.950
about.

00:26:47.950 --> 00:26:52.620
Thankfully it never gained much political
support but its ideas remained ever present

00:26:52.620 --> 00:26:56.990
in Hungarian politics and strongly entrenched
in the Hungarian military.

00:26:56.990 --> 00:27:02.660
Horthy in the early 1920s also had several
plans to reconquer primarily Transylvania

00:27:02.660 --> 00:27:07.680
and Slovakia but these never went anywhere
as most Hungarian politicians were against

00:27:07.680 --> 00:27:12.740
any military actions considering their neighbors
had military support from the entente and

00:27:12.740 --> 00:27:15.460
Hungary's economic situation was very poor.

00:27:15.460 --> 00:27:19.440
This is not to say that the Hungarian politicians
didn’t want to restore original Hungarian

00:27:19.440 --> 00:27:25.330
borders, they just were hoping to do it diplomatically
through revising the Trianon treaty, not through

00:27:25.330 --> 00:27:26.980
yet another war.

00:27:26.980 --> 00:27:33.310
Plus, Hungary had one more major problem to
deal with in 1921 and that was the return

00:27:33.310 --> 00:27:37.310
of the Habsburg king Karl the IV.

00:27:37.310 --> 00:27:40.565
Biography of Miklós Horthy : The Return of
the King

00:27:40.565 --> 00:27:44.990
Horthy was sporadically communicating with
Karl during the entire post war period and

00:27:44.990 --> 00:27:49.610
during their communications he never gave
any sign that would suggest he would not give

00:27:49.610 --> 00:27:52.180
up the throne to Karl if he returned.

00:27:52.180 --> 00:27:56.290
Plus Horthy still saw himself as a loyal subject
of the emperor.

00:27:56.290 --> 00:28:02.140
But, the roughly one year period of Horthy’s
regency between 1920 and 21 gave Horthy a

00:28:02.140 --> 00:28:07.450
taste for power, for control, and for being
able to do something to help Hungary.

00:28:07.450 --> 00:28:13.140
Horthy came to increasingly see himself as
someone who could help and fix Hungary if

00:28:13.140 --> 00:28:19.870
only he stayed in power, and so, when, Karl
unexpectedly came to Hungary, to retake his

00:28:19.870 --> 00:28:23.010
throne, Horthy went through a serious internal
crisis.

00:28:23.010 --> 00:28:29.090
It also didn’t help that the Hungarian parliament
was at the time also divided between “legitimists”

00:28:29.090 --> 00:28:33.060
supporting the return of Karl von Habsburg
and the “free-electors” supporting the

00:28:33.060 --> 00:28:36.970
election of an official Hungarian king e.g.
Horthy.

00:28:36.970 --> 00:28:43.630
In essence, Karl's arrival in Hungary split
both the loyalties of parliament, and of Horthy’s

00:28:43.630 --> 00:28:44.630
conscience.

00:28:44.630 --> 00:28:49.230
Karl, however, remained convinced that the
old admiral would keep his promise he made

00:28:49.230 --> 00:28:51.050
to him in 1918.

00:28:51.050 --> 00:28:55.780
Karl also allegedly secured a verbal promise
from the French prime minister that France

00:28:55.780 --> 00:28:58.860
would support habsburg restoration in Hungary.

00:28:58.860 --> 00:29:03.350
Armed with the belief that Horthy was going
to relinquish power to him and that the French

00:29:03.350 --> 00:29:09.160
would support him Karl, without a large entourage
nor much planning, suddenly showed up at the

00:29:09.160 --> 00:29:13.550
royal palace in Budapest 27th of March 1921.

00:29:13.550 --> 00:29:19.880
Horthy was told about Karl only minutes before
his arrival and was in vivid turmoil.

00:29:19.880 --> 00:29:24.360
One of Horthy’s bodyguards noticed this
and in the hopes of encouraging the regent

00:29:24.360 --> 00:29:28.740
said “The Guard will be faithful until death
to the Regent.

00:29:28.740 --> 00:29:33.980
In the name of the Magyar nation we ask the
Regent to remain true to the oath he has taken

00:29:33.980 --> 00:29:35.060
to the nation.”

00:29:35.060 --> 00:29:41.820
Minutes after that, Karl and Horthy were sitting
in the main office of the royal palace and,

00:29:41.820 --> 00:29:47.260
what Horthy described as “the most difficult
moments in my entire life”, began.

00:29:47.260 --> 00:29:52.310
Horthy admitted the throne should belong to
Karl and that he was still a loyal servant

00:29:52.310 --> 00:29:57.800
of the emperor but, at the same time, Horthy
also believed he was a better choice to lead

00:29:57.800 --> 00:30:03.680
the Hungarian nation at this specific time
and that, if Karl took the throne, Hungary

00:30:03.680 --> 00:30:09.080
would be occupied on all sides by its neighbors
who were supported by the entente which already

00:30:09.080 --> 00:30:12.480
stated it didn’t want Habsburg restoration.

00:30:12.480 --> 00:30:16.630
Despite being a loyal servant of the emperor,
Horthy could not let this happen.

00:30:16.630 --> 00:30:22.100
When Horthy declined to relinquish power Karl
asked “You would disobey a command of your

00:30:22.100 --> 00:30:23.100
King?”

00:30:23.100 --> 00:30:28.320
Horthy, clearly unnerved by this statement,
didn't reply, and continued to argue that

00:30:28.320 --> 00:30:30.600
it was impossible for Karl to take the throne.

00:30:30.600 --> 00:30:36.160
“There is not even a one-half percent possibility
that your Majesty will succeed.”

00:30:36.160 --> 00:30:41.330
Brushing these arguments aside Karl continued
to question Horthy’s loyalties but the regent

00:30:41.330 --> 00:30:42.640
would not yield.

00:30:42.640 --> 00:30:47.550
Finally, to address the regents' concern with
the entente, Karl mentioned that he had the

00:30:47.550 --> 00:30:52.240
support of the French prime minister but he
could not prove it for it was only given to

00:30:52.240 --> 00:30:53.250
him verbally.

00:30:53.250 --> 00:30:58.080
Horthy was very skeptical of this and continued
to refuse to relinquish power.

00:30:58.080 --> 00:31:04.340
After an almost 3 hour debate Horthy concluded
with “Your Majesty, I must choose between

00:31:04.340 --> 00:31:07.280
my loyalty to the dynasty and to my nation.

00:31:07.280 --> 00:31:12.630
I choose the nation, and will not hand over
the government, because in twenty-four hours

00:31:12.630 --> 00:31:16.410
this unfortunate country would be occupied
and partitioned.”

00:31:16.410 --> 00:31:22.910
With that, the conversation ended, and a deeply
saddened Karl departed the palace, but he

00:31:22.910 --> 00:31:23.970
did not leave Hungary.

00:31:23.970 --> 00:31:29.530
The next day Karl sent a message to Horthy
stating “I demand that you immediately submit

00:31:29.530 --> 00:31:36.550
yourself to my command, I have no doubts,
my dear, faithful admiral, about your response.”

00:31:36.550 --> 00:31:41.280
Horthy responded “I cannot oppose my king
… pushed into a conflict of conscience I

00:31:41.280 --> 00:31:46.770
shall be forced to resign: that is why I ask
for the withdrawal of this order.”

00:31:46.770 --> 00:31:52.120
Karl, however, did not withdraw his order
and the regent did not resign.

00:31:52.120 --> 00:31:57.250
The following days, as the word got out that
Karl was back in Hungary, the entente diplomats

00:31:57.250 --> 00:32:02.900
in Budapest all reaffirmed they will not support
Habsburg restoration in Hungary, and the neighboring

00:32:02.900 --> 00:32:08.450
countries, confirming Horthy’s fears, stated
that a return of a Habsburg rule would give

00:32:08.450 --> 00:32:09.980
them a casus belli.

00:32:09.980 --> 00:32:15.730
The alleged French support for Karl never
materialized and so even the legitimists seeing

00:32:15.730 --> 00:32:20.270
that a peaceful restoration of the Habsburg
monarchy wouldn’t be possible started to

00:32:20.270 --> 00:32:22.080
withdraw their support.

00:32:22.080 --> 00:32:26.480
In the end, Karl had no choice but to leave
Hungary in April.

00:32:26.480 --> 00:32:32.890
Horthy could finally breathe a sigh of relief,
but not for long, as Karl returned to Hungary

00:32:32.890 --> 00:32:35.620
20th of October that same year.

00:32:35.620 --> 00:32:38.680
This time hoping to take the throne by military
means.

00:32:38.680 --> 00:32:44.220
This was to be the last hurrah for the remaining
Hungarian legitimists who started off in Sopron

00:32:44.220 --> 00:32:47.670
and continued to gather supporters on their
march to Budapest.

00:32:47.670 --> 00:32:52.130
Horthy again argued that he couldn't give
up the throne because if he did Hungary would

00:32:52.130 --> 00:32:55.480
be destroyed in a war with the entente and
its neighbors.

00:32:55.480 --> 00:33:00.500
Therefore, he, along with the free-electors
in the parliament, tried to quickly mobilize

00:33:00.500 --> 00:33:05.660
a defense of the capital with Horthy proclaiming
he will defend Budapest against “our poor

00:33:05.660 --> 00:33:08.250
king who has been led astray”.

00:33:08.250 --> 00:33:13.300
Seeing this as a serious military threat neighboring
countries partially mobilized some of their

00:33:13.300 --> 00:33:18.090
troops, most notably Czechoslovakia who was
poised to “exploit the crisis to deal a

00:33:18.090 --> 00:33:22.120
crushing blow to nationalist and irredentist
sentiment in Hungary”.

00:33:22.120 --> 00:33:27.360
The entente yet again stated their strong
opposition to any Habsburg rule in Hungary

00:33:27.360 --> 00:33:30.790
while also denouncing the intentions of Czechoslovakia.

00:33:30.790 --> 00:33:36.110
Karl, seeing that he had no international
support and that his restoration could spark

00:33:36.110 --> 00:33:42.040
not just a civil war in Hungary but also an
all out war with its neighbors, finally gave

00:33:42.040 --> 00:33:43.040
up.

00:33:43.040 --> 00:33:46.000
He left Hungary in November for the last time,
defeated.

00:33:46.000 --> 00:33:51.610
The free-electors now in control of the parliament
imposed their will and in November a law was

00:33:51.610 --> 00:33:56.560
passed effectively dethroning the Habsburg
dynasty from the Hungarian throne.

00:33:56.560 --> 00:34:02.550
Hungary still remained a kingdom, with a regent,
waiting for a king; however, now that the

00:34:02.550 --> 00:34:08.369
habsburgs were effectively dethroned, who
was to be this king of Hungary exactly was

00:34:08.369 --> 00:34:09.820
never determined.

00:34:09.820 --> 00:34:14.669
This was mainly due to the fact that the old
conservative monarchist system which Horthy

00:34:14.669 --> 00:34:18.780
and his parliament implemented, and which
did not differ much from the system of the

00:34:18.780 --> 00:34:25.290
old empire, was keeping the status quo and
the old aristocracy intact, and so, in turn,

00:34:25.290 --> 00:34:30.630
the old aristocracy, who was largely in charge,
did not mess with the system that kept them

00:34:30.630 --> 00:34:31.840
in charge.

00:34:31.840 --> 00:34:36.760
Electing Horthy as an official king might
have upset the balance in the country and

00:34:36.760 --> 00:34:42.419
in Central Europe as a whole and so, the status
quo of having a “regent” who was effectively

00:34:42.419 --> 00:34:45.250
the king in all but name was never changed.

00:34:45.250 --> 00:34:51.300
Therefore, it wasn’t unsurprising when in
1929 Count Bethlen, the then prime minister

00:34:51.300 --> 00:34:56.500
of Hungary, proclaimed that “Horthy would
remain in office to the end of his life”.

00:34:56.500 --> 00:35:01.510
Horthy and his old conservative parliament
believed that a full democracy would be a

00:35:01.510 --> 00:35:08.050
disaster, a rule of the mob, and so implemented
a system where only 28% of the population,

00:35:08.050 --> 00:35:11.340
mostly the upper and upper middle class, was
eligible to vote.

00:35:11.340 --> 00:35:15.780
This meant that old conservative parties could
remain largely in charge of the parliament

00:35:15.780 --> 00:35:20.270
during the interwar period and the aristocracy
remained in control of most of the country's

00:35:20.270 --> 00:35:21.850
land and industry (along with rich industrialists).

00:35:21.850 --> 00:35:25.180
This system was called by some a “semi-feudal
order”.

00:35:25.180 --> 00:35:30.690
Horthy, himself, was also often called having
“an almost medieval mentality” who often

00:35:30.690 --> 00:35:35.390
revald in his leader’s cult which compared
him to such medieval Hungarian figures like

00:35:35.390 --> 00:35:36.780
John Hunyadi.

00:35:36.780 --> 00:35:42.010
To give an example of Horthy’s medieval
mentality; during one comedic affair, when

00:35:42.010 --> 00:35:47.900
in 1936 some Czechoslovak newspapers published
some slednoures articles about Hungary, Horthy,

00:35:47.900 --> 00:35:53.640
to defend his nation's honor, challenged Masaryk,
the then president of Czechoslovakia, to a

00:35:53.640 --> 00:35:54.640
duel.

00:35:54.640 --> 00:35:58.610
This obviously did not happen but it goes
to show that Horthy was often stuck in his

00:35:58.610 --> 00:36:00.290
19th century ways.

00:36:00.290 --> 00:36:05.640
With all that said, despite Horthy’s championing
of old conservatism and his dissociation with

00:36:05.640 --> 00:36:10.640
the right-wing radicals in the early 1920s,
the undercurrent of radical right-wing movements

00:36:10.640 --> 00:36:12.850
never really went away in Hungary.

00:36:12.850 --> 00:36:18.330
Horthy never actually tried to stomp out the
right-wing radicals and on occasions even

00:36:18.330 --> 00:36:23.420
tolerated their presence, especially in the
military, which proved highly problematic

00:36:23.420 --> 00:36:25.619
by the time of the second world war.

00:36:25.619 --> 00:36:30.290
Biography of Miklós Horthy : The Two Sides

00:36:30.290 --> 00:36:36.330
When it came to the late 1930s Horthy was
presented with multiple, all partially unwelcome

00:36:36.330 --> 00:36:37.540
opportunities.

00:36:37.540 --> 00:36:42.180
He was happy seeing the rise of fascisim across
Europe which, despite not agreeing with its

00:36:42.180 --> 00:36:47.550
values fully, he saw as a far more favorable
political movement than communism.

00:36:47.550 --> 00:36:52.500
However, the rise of fascism in his own country
and the creation of the Arrow Cross, was a

00:36:52.500 --> 00:36:54.290
highly unwelcomed one.

00:36:54.290 --> 00:37:00.300
In Horthy’s eyes they were far too radical,
far too anti-semetic, and far too in favor

00:37:00.300 --> 00:37:05.710
of a military dictatorship which would upend
the centuries old Hungarian semi-feudal order.

00:37:05.710 --> 00:37:11.150
Horthy also had some gripes when it came to
Hitler himself, a man “whose vulgarity and

00:37:11.150 --> 00:37:15.050
histrionic ways were hardly the marks of a
true gentleman”.

00:37:15.050 --> 00:37:20.231
Despite all these gripes, Hitler tried to
entice Horthy by presenting him with the opportunity

00:37:20.231 --> 00:37:22.800
to restore the original borders of Hungary.

00:37:22.800 --> 00:37:27.860
Horthy was extremely pleased with this opportunity
but also extremely cautious.

00:37:27.860 --> 00:37:33.010
Being an old admiral he never for a second
believed, if a world war was to break out,

00:37:33.010 --> 00:37:38.390
that Nazy Germany could ever beat Britain
and USA who had much superior navies.

00:37:38.390 --> 00:37:41.510
He even made this known to Hitler on multiple
occasions.

00:37:41.510 --> 00:37:46.230
Horthy was instead hoping that if Hungary
was to restore its original borders it would

00:37:46.230 --> 00:37:50.510
do so not just with German support but also
with allied support.

00:37:50.510 --> 00:37:55.220
This was obviously quickly shot down by both
the allies and Nazy Germany.

00:37:55.220 --> 00:37:59.840
With Horthy’s plan of both German and Allied
support for the restoration of Hungarian borders

00:37:59.840 --> 00:38:01.820
not materializing.

00:38:01.820 --> 00:38:04.850
Hungary started to be politically pulled apart.

00:38:04.850 --> 00:38:08.780
Hungarian politics became increasingly divided
between the “German Sympathizers”, who

00:38:08.780 --> 00:38:13.450
wanted to use an alliance with Nazy Germany
to restore Hungarian borders and defeat the

00:38:13.450 --> 00:38:18.660
Soviets, and the Hungarian “Neutralists”
who, even though also wanting to restore Hungarian

00:38:18.660 --> 00:38:24.760
borders, believed Nazy Germany was going to
lose the inevitable world war, and, therefore,

00:38:24.760 --> 00:38:29.550
wanted to remain neutral waiting for a more
opportune moment for the restoration of Hungarian

00:38:29.550 --> 00:38:30.550
borders.

00:38:30.550 --> 00:38:34.830
Of course, there is far more to this divide
than just the way Hungarians wanted to restore

00:38:34.830 --> 00:38:39.920
their original borders, the neutralists, who
were mostly the old conservatives, also didn’t

00:38:39.920 --> 00:38:44.880
like the rampant German antisemitism and over
all prefered closer ties with the west.

00:38:44.880 --> 00:38:49.950
While the German sympathizers were mostly
Hungarian fascists and other right-wing radicals

00:38:49.950 --> 00:38:53.480
who wanted to implement many Nazy style laws
in Hungary.

00:38:53.480 --> 00:38:58.800
To the dismay of the Hungarian fascists and
the German sympathizers Horthy sided yet again

00:38:58.800 --> 00:39:03.860
with the old conservatives and for much of
the pre war period pursued a tactic of neutrality.

00:39:03.860 --> 00:39:09.410
When Nazy Germany was getting ready to invade
Czechoslovakia Hitler told Horthy that if

00:39:09.410 --> 00:39:14.470
Hungary was to aid in a possible invasion
it could take the whole of Slovakia.

00:39:14.470 --> 00:39:19.190
Even though delighted at the prospect of this,
Horthy declined the offer, fearing that it

00:39:19.190 --> 00:39:23.720
would force Hungary into an alliance with
the Axis who would be fighting a losing war

00:39:23.720 --> 00:39:25.050
against the allies.

00:39:25.050 --> 00:39:29.730
Horthy even told the British and American
ambassadors in Budapest that Hitler was a

00:39:29.730 --> 00:39:32.610
“madman who was bringing the world to chaos.”

00:39:32.610 --> 00:39:37.320
With all that said, Hungary did gain Southern
Slovakia thanks to the First Vienna Award

00:39:37.320 --> 00:39:39.940
which was a conclusion to the Munich Agreement.

00:39:39.940 --> 00:39:45.690
The Munich agreement was, however, an internationally
recognized treaty, and even though largely

00:39:45.690 --> 00:39:50.680
negotiated by the Germans, Horthy and his
neutralist allies made sure to make it clear

00:39:50.680 --> 00:39:57.010
that Hungary negotiated its part of the agreement
alone and not in partnership with the Nazis.

00:39:57.010 --> 00:40:01.240
In essence Horthy and the neutralists were
using the political situation in Europe to

00:40:01.240 --> 00:40:07.020
their benefit while keeping the Nazis at arms
lenght to secure their neutrality.

00:40:07.020 --> 00:40:11.250
Hungary employed the same tactic, of keeping
German involvement at arms length, a couple

00:40:11.250 --> 00:40:15.750
of months later when they annexed Ruthenia
during the German invasion of Czechia and

00:40:15.750 --> 00:40:18.200
the proclamation of independent Slovakia.

00:40:18.200 --> 00:40:23.010
This was met with greater international opposition
than the annexation of Southern Slovakia as

00:40:23.010 --> 00:40:27.670
it wasn’t part of the Munich agreement but
for the most part, with Germany supporting

00:40:27.670 --> 00:40:31.510
the action, Hungary did not see much international
backlash.

00:40:31.510 --> 00:40:36.960
Again, just like with Southern Slovakia, Hungary
could only do this because of the actiaons

00:40:36.960 --> 00:40:42.770
of Nazy Germany, but again, Horthy and the
neutralists only exploited the political situation

00:40:42.770 --> 00:40:48.610
which the Nazis created, withou actually directly
working with the Nazis and sometimes even

00:40:48.610 --> 00:40:49.760
opposing them.

00:40:49.760 --> 00:40:54.260
This opposition can, for example, be seen
when the Nazis asked if Hungary was to help

00:40:54.260 --> 00:40:59.160
them invade Poland or at least let German
troops travel through Hungary, to which Horthy

00:40:59.160 --> 00:41:03.960
allegedly replied he would rather blow up
his own rail-lines than let the Germans use

00:41:03.960 --> 00:41:04.960
them.

00:41:04.960 --> 00:41:08.880
All this political maneuvering of Horthy and
the neutralists, of trying to keep Hungary

00:41:08.880 --> 00:41:14.800
neutral while exploiting the situation, was
becoming ever more controversial in Hungary.

00:41:14.800 --> 00:41:19.540
Sure Hungary did gain some land but that paled
in comparison to what it could have gotten

00:41:19.540 --> 00:41:24.440
if it just cooperated with Germany fully,
and due to this the Hungarian fascists and

00:41:24.440 --> 00:41:27.490
the German sympathizers were gaining ever
more power.

00:41:27.490 --> 00:41:32.359
Plus, after the German victory in Poland and
later in western Europe, even some of the

00:41:32.359 --> 00:41:36.190
neutralists started to doubt the neutrality
stance Hungary had taken.

00:41:36.190 --> 00:41:41.690
Then, when Romania was weakened due to being
forced to succeed Bessarabia to the Soviets,

00:41:41.690 --> 00:41:46.280
the largely fascist army officers in Hungary
started to pressure Horthy and the neutralists

00:41:46.280 --> 00:41:47.890
to take Transilvania.

00:41:47.890 --> 00:41:50.490
For now was the time, Romania was weak.

00:41:50.490 --> 00:41:54.320
They even began to prepare the Hungarian army
for an attack.

00:41:54.320 --> 00:41:56.970
This entire situation made Hitler furious.

00:41:56.970 --> 00:42:02.070
He could not allow Hungary to instigate a
conflict with Romania who he viewed as a valuable

00:42:02.070 --> 00:42:04.720
ally for a future attack on the USSR.

00:42:04.720 --> 00:42:08.270
Therefore, he offered to arbitrate the whole
situation.

00:42:08.270 --> 00:42:12.530
Subsequently the Second Vienna Award occurred
and Romania was forced to give up northern

00:42:12.530 --> 00:42:15.290
Transylvania in order to appease Hungary.

00:42:15.290 --> 00:42:20.430
Yet again were the Hungarian fascists and
German sympathizers proven correct.

00:42:20.430 --> 00:42:25.460
If only Hungary was to just work directly
with Germany it could gain so much more.

00:42:25.460 --> 00:42:30.550
This affair also showed that Horthy was losing
control over his ever growing radicalized

00:42:30.550 --> 00:42:34.740
army which was the main instigator of this
entire clash.

00:42:34.740 --> 00:42:40.609
All these events came to a head in 1941 when
Hitler effectively manipulated Horthy.

00:42:40.609 --> 00:42:46.980
Hitler knew that Horthy, an old admiral, always
had dreams of establishing a Hungarian port.

00:42:46.980 --> 00:42:51.960
So, playing on these dreams, Hitler proposed
that if Hungary was to help in conquering

00:42:51.960 --> 00:42:56.780
Yugoslavia he would negotiate with the Italians
to give Hungary a port in Croatia.

00:42:56.780 --> 00:43:01.820
Horthy was so enthused by this prospect that
he could not be stopped even by his neutralist

00:43:01.820 --> 00:43:04.770
allies from making Hungary partake in this
war.

00:43:04.770 --> 00:43:09.521
The old conservatives pleaded with the regent,
they tried to convince him that this was a

00:43:09.521 --> 00:43:11.430
terrible mistake.

00:43:11.430 --> 00:43:16.119
After all, he himself believed that Germany
could not win this world war.

00:43:16.119 --> 00:43:21.590
However, Horthy’s military staff and other
German sympathizers argued that this was finally

00:43:21.590 --> 00:43:24.930
the chance for Hungary to retake its southern
lands back.

00:43:24.930 --> 00:43:26.110
To gain a port.

00:43:26.110 --> 00:43:30.770
In the end, Horthy could not be stopped from
his dream of acquiring a port for Hungary

00:43:30.770 --> 00:43:34.850
and so approved Hungarian involvement in the
Yugoslav war.

00:43:34.850 --> 00:43:39.140
This meant that Hungary was to finally go
to war alongside Germany.

00:43:39.140 --> 00:43:45.270
The Hungarian fascists and German sympathizers,
despite still being opposed by Horthy, finally

00:43:45.270 --> 00:43:49.760
got what they wanted and enthusiastically
supported the regent’s decision.

00:43:49.760 --> 00:43:54.940
The years of neutrality that the neutralists
have been trying to cultivate were shattered

00:43:54.940 --> 00:43:57.560
by the fascists and Horthy’s ambition.

00:43:57.560 --> 00:44:02.240
The prime minister of Hungary at the time,
Teleki, who was a neutralist staunchly against

00:44:02.240 --> 00:44:07.740
siding with Germany stated that “My situation
is extremely difficult, because the regent,

00:44:07.740 --> 00:44:12.570
the army, half of the government, and the
parliamentary majority are against me”.

00:44:12.570 --> 00:44:17.580
He tried everything he could to keep Hungary
out of the war but in the end he failed.

00:44:17.580 --> 00:44:20.380
This failure made him go into deep depression.

00:44:20.380 --> 00:44:26.010
He could not bear to see his country go into
yet another world war alongside Germany which

00:44:26.010 --> 00:44:28.030
he believed couldn’t be trusted.

00:44:28.030 --> 00:44:32.520
Due to this he committed suicide right before
the invasion of Yugoslavia.

00:44:32.520 --> 00:44:39.030
His suicide note read “We have become breakers
of our word - out of cowardice - in defiance

00:44:39.030 --> 00:44:42.820
of the Treaty of eternal friendship based
on the Mohacs speech.

00:44:42.820 --> 00:44:46.840
The nation feels this, and we have thrown
away its honor.

00:44:46.840 --> 00:44:53.090
We have placed ourselves on the side of scoundrels,
for there is not a word of truth in the stories

00:44:53.090 --> 00:44:57.119
of atrocities against the Magyars or the Germans
[in Yugoslavia].

00:44:57.119 --> 00:45:02.760
We shall become the despoilers of corpses,
the most abominable of nations!

00:45:02.760 --> 00:45:04.910
I did not restrain you [Hungary].

00:45:04.910 --> 00:45:06.660
I am guilty.”

00:45:06.660 --> 00:45:12.500
Horthy was shaken by Teleki’s sucide but,
nonetheless, still believed he made the right

00:45:12.500 --> 00:45:13.500
decision.

00:45:13.500 --> 00:45:17.750
After the successful invasion of Yugoslavia
Hungary did gain some territory from the campaign

00:45:17.750 --> 00:45:20.640
but by far not as much as Horthy was hoping.

00:45:20.640 --> 00:45:25.760
It was partially due to this that, when the
German invasion of the USSR began, Horthy

00:45:25.760 --> 00:45:29.690
initially did not support it and did not declare
war on the USSR.

00:45:29.690 --> 00:45:34.580
But, the fascist movement in Hungary was too
strong at this point and the new fascist prime

00:45:34.580 --> 00:45:39.350
minister László Bárdossy, along with the
fascists in the military, convinced Horthy

00:45:39.350 --> 00:45:44.390
that it would be in Hungary's best interest
to declare war against the USSR.

00:45:44.390 --> 00:45:49.590
Convincing Horthy of this, actually, wasn’t
very hard as he was a staunch anti-communist

00:45:49.590 --> 00:45:54.170
since the time of the Hungarian Soviet Republic
and Bárdossy presented the war to the regent

00:45:54.170 --> 00:45:58.859
as an “old crusade against bolshevism”
which Horthy very much liked the sound of.

00:45:58.859 --> 00:46:03.980
and so, Hungary was going to war alongside
Nazy Germany again.

00:46:03.980 --> 00:46:10.280
Win or lose, Hungary’s fate was now unquestionably
tied to that of Nazy Germany.

00:46:10.280 --> 00:46:15.109
Even though the fate of Hungary was now tied
to Nazi Germany, Horthy still seemed to have,

00:46:15.109 --> 00:46:19.369
in the back of his mind, believed in the superiority
of the allied navy.

00:46:19.369 --> 00:46:23.600
Britain had broken off diplomatic relations
with Hungary at this point but America had

00:46:23.600 --> 00:46:28.490
not, as it wasn’t in the war yet, and Horthy
invited the American ambassador in 1941 for

00:46:28.490 --> 00:46:33.280
friendly meals during which he would talk
to him about the “Anglo-Saxon powers”

00:46:33.280 --> 00:46:35.210
and their navy and industry.

00:46:35.210 --> 00:46:39.840
Horthy’s prais of the “Anglo-Saxon powers”,
while being at war with some of them, goes

00:46:39.840 --> 00:46:45.020
to show just how much Hungary, and Horthy
himself, was politically divided.

00:46:45.020 --> 00:46:49.480
Horthy still seemed to have garnered some
sympathies for the western allies.

00:46:49.480 --> 00:46:53.550
On the other hand Horthy could not ignore
the very strong fascist movement in Hungary

00:46:53.550 --> 00:46:57.260
or the fact that Hungary was in no position
to oppose Nazi Germany.

00:46:57.260 --> 00:47:01.650
If Hungary didn’t go to war willingly with
Nazi Germany it would certainly be forced

00:47:01.650 --> 00:47:02.650
go.

00:47:02.650 --> 00:47:07.109
On top of that Horthy viewed the war with
the USSR as separate from the war with the

00:47:07.109 --> 00:47:08.109
Western Powers.

00:47:08.109 --> 00:47:12.300
In his eyes, the war against the Soviet Union
should have been supported by the west as

00:47:12.300 --> 00:47:16.760
he was fighting against the “power that
intends to destroy civilization”.

00:47:16.760 --> 00:47:21.580
In contrast to that, the war with the western
powers, which later also included the US,

00:47:21.580 --> 00:47:26.490
was a misunderstanding that he hoped could
be solved with “some sort of compromise

00:47:26.490 --> 00:47:27.490
peace”.

00:47:27.490 --> 00:47:33.160
Therefore, when Hungary, in accordance with
Nazi Germany, declared war on the US in December

00:47:33.160 --> 00:47:38.770
of 1941, Horthy was absolutly devasted and
furious, for he did not approve this declaration

00:47:38.770 --> 00:47:42.410
of war and it was solely done by the prime
minister Bárdossy.

00:47:42.410 --> 00:47:47.570
Before the departure of the US embassy from
Hungary Horthy’s son, Istvan, “expressed

00:47:47.570 --> 00:47:51.710
the sympathy for the Allies that both he and
his father felt”.

00:47:51.710 --> 00:47:56.830
With all that said, the initial victories
of Germany against the allies made even Horthy

00:47:56.830 --> 00:48:03.020
start to doubt his own belief in the “Anglo-Saxon
powers” and made him, weirdly, for a brief

00:48:03.020 --> 00:48:09.300
moment, hold contradicting beliefs in both
Axis and Western Allied victory.

00:48:09.300 --> 00:48:14.070
When it came to the jewish question during
this time, Hungary was yet again strongly

00:48:14.070 --> 00:48:15.070
divided.

00:48:15.070 --> 00:48:19.320
The old conservatives, along with Horthy,
even though holding some antisemtic views

00:48:19.320 --> 00:48:24.470
themselves, were not willing to implement
the extremely harsh anti-jewish laws of the

00:48:24.470 --> 00:48:25.470
fascists.

00:48:25.470 --> 00:48:28.770
Ironically the Hungarian upper house, the
Hungarian version of the house of lords, (Főrendiház,

00:48:28.770 --> 00:48:32.580
House of Magnates), which was criticized for
keeping the “semi-feudal order” of hungary

00:48:32.580 --> 00:48:37.859
intact during the interwar period, now thwarted
the enactment of harsh antisemtic laws by

00:48:37.859 --> 00:48:41.050
the right-wing anti-semits in the Hungarian
lower house (Képviselőház, House of Representatives).

00:48:41.050 --> 00:48:45.140
All of this is not to say that the parliament
did not implement antisemetic laws during

00:48:45.140 --> 00:48:47.080
this time, it definitely did.

00:48:47.080 --> 00:48:51.849
For example, Hungarians deported some jews
to Nazy Germany who did not have Hungarian

00:48:51.849 --> 00:48:56.570
citizenship, they forcibly relocated or even
killed some jews living in the newly conquered

00:48:56.570 --> 00:49:01.790
border areas to strengthen the areas “ethnic
make-up”, and they confiscated some jewish

00:49:01.790 --> 00:49:03.220
property, etc.

00:49:03.220 --> 00:49:07.790
But they also protected most Hungarian jews
from being deported to Nazy Germany, or being

00:49:07.790 --> 00:49:11.910
used as forced laborers, or being killed just
for being jewish.

00:49:11.910 --> 00:49:16.770
Most of these legislations, both good and
bad, were either signed off by Horthy or not

00:49:16.770 --> 00:49:18.720
suspensory vetoed by him.

00:49:18.720 --> 00:49:23.280
This quote by Horthy perhaps best summarizes
his views on the situation and the overall

00:49:23.280 --> 00:49:28.430
sentiment of the old conservatives towards
the jews ”I have perhaps been the first

00:49:28.430 --> 00:49:34.310
to loudly profess anti-Semetism, yet I cannot
look with indifference at the inhumanity and

00:49:34.310 --> 00:49:37.910
senseless humiliations when we still need
them.

00:49:37.910 --> 00:49:43.331
Moreover, I consider, for example, the Arrowcross
men [and other right-wing radicals] to be

00:49:43.331 --> 00:49:48.201
by far more dangerous and worthless for my
country than I do the Jew.

00:49:48.201 --> 00:49:53.790
The latter is tied to this country from self-interest,
and is more faithful to his adopted country

00:49:53.790 --> 00:49:59.020
than the Arrowcross men, who … with their
muddled brains want to play the country into

00:49:59.020 --> 00:50:02.030
the hands of the Germans.”

00:50:02.030 --> 00:50:06.640
Also during this time, while the war was going
well, Horthy, after having a couple of health

00:50:06.640 --> 00:50:11.150
scares at the age of 74, started to worry
about the succession of the regency.

00:50:11.150 --> 00:50:16.369
He was convinced that the next regent should
be his eldest son, Istvan Horthy, who he viewed

00:50:16.369 --> 00:50:17.510
as a genius.

00:50:17.510 --> 00:50:22.510
It was true that his son was very knowledgeable
and had extensive managerial skills but he

00:50:22.510 --> 00:50:27.650
also lacked any political or military skills,
plus, he was viewed by a lot of the Hungarian

00:50:27.650 --> 00:50:32.440
politicians as a quote “liberal playboy”
who was the worst of both worlds.

00:50:32.440 --> 00:50:37.960
The old conservatives viewed him as too liberal
and too willing to enact certain social reforms,

00:50:37.960 --> 00:50:43.930
the socialists saw him as a conservative aristocrat,
the fascists viewed him as too socialist,

00:50:43.930 --> 00:50:49.150
and, worst of all, he held no antisemitic
views which was unacceptable in an age of

00:50:49.150 --> 00:50:51.460
rampant antisemitism.

00:50:51.460 --> 00:50:56.480
Despite all this, Horthy did manage to get
his son elected in 1942, with few caveats,

00:50:56.480 --> 00:50:57.660
as a Deputy Regent.

00:50:57.660 --> 00:51:03.190
So, for a brief moment, the succession question
seemed to have been resolved but, that same

00:51:03.190 --> 00:51:06.230
year, Istvan would sadly die on the eastern
front.

00:51:06.230 --> 00:51:11.230
After Istvan’s death, Horthy’s second
eldest son, Miklos Horthy junior, became the

00:51:11.230 --> 00:51:16.580
next candidate for the Deputy Regent position,
but considering the now ever worsening state

00:51:16.580 --> 00:51:20.690
on the eastern front, more pressing matters
had to be attended to first.

00:51:20.690 --> 00:51:25.480
As the war started to turn against Germany
and in doing so also against Hungary.

00:51:25.480 --> 00:51:30.690
Horthy’s belief in the “anglo-saxon powers”
and his disdain for Nazy Germany and Hitler

00:51:30.690 --> 00:51:32.480
returned in full force.

00:51:32.480 --> 00:51:37.240
Horthy quickly allied himself with the neutralists
once again and started trying to regain some

00:51:37.240 --> 00:51:41.060
favor with the allies by beginning secret
peace talks with them.

00:51:41.060 --> 00:51:44.920
He, however, made sure to exclude the Soviet
Union from these talks.

00:51:44.920 --> 00:51:49.470
Horthy, along with all the other Hungarian
politicians, feared that if the USSR gained

00:51:49.470 --> 00:51:54.200
control of post war Hungary that “was bound
to mean the end of Hungary, for it was quite

00:51:54.200 --> 00:51:59.740
natural that as a drop in the ocean of Bolshevik
and Slav peoples the Hungarian identity would

00:51:59.740 --> 00:52:00.740
disappear.”

00:52:00.740 --> 00:52:05.730
Therefore, Horthy tried his utmost to gain
whatever favor he could with the west, primarily

00:52:05.730 --> 00:52:07.570
Brittain and the USA.

00:52:07.570 --> 00:52:11.980
Britain and the US, with their preparation
for D-day, put pressure on Hungary to rebel

00:52:11.980 --> 00:52:16.690
against German control and in doing so divert
German resources.

00:52:16.690 --> 00:52:21.490
The allies insisted that Hungary “should
immediately follow Italy’s example (i.e.

00:52:21.490 --> 00:52:23.810
jump out) shouldering the risks.

00:52:23.810 --> 00:52:28.160
If Hungary failed to draw the consequences
of this situation it would mean that it was

00:52:28.160 --> 00:52:30.370
once more siding with the Germans.

00:52:30.370 --> 00:52:35.090
It would thereby forever lose her chance of
being handled differently from Germany by

00:52:35.090 --> 00:52:39.470
the victors … [Hungary] should take this
step even at the risk of temporary German

00:52:39.470 --> 00:52:40.470
occupation.”

00:52:40.470 --> 00:52:45.599
When Horthy along with his politicians voiced
concerns of “The possible ramifications

00:52:45.599 --> 00:52:51.320
of German invasion: the destruction of Hungarian
democratic elements and Europe’s last intact

00:52:51.320 --> 00:52:55.840
Jewish community” the allied negotiators
replied ”there is a war on, we are up to

00:52:55.840 --> 00:53:02.359
our necks in blood, a few hundred thousand
lives here and there will not make a difference.”

00:53:02.359 --> 00:53:06.620
All these negotiations were caught by the
German secret service and in order to keep

00:53:06.620 --> 00:53:12.030
Hungary loyal, and in the war, Hitler invaded
Hungary in March of 1944.

00:53:12.030 --> 00:53:17.200
Hungary did not fight back against the Germans
as many Hungarian fascists welcomed the regime

00:53:17.200 --> 00:53:21.980
change and Horthy knew that Hungary had no
chance of defeating the German army so he

00:53:21.980 --> 00:53:23.590
didn’t try to fight it.

00:53:23.590 --> 00:53:28.349
Horthy also came to a tenuous agreement with
Hitler where he will still remain in power

00:53:28.349 --> 00:53:30.869
even if as a figurehead for the Germans.

00:53:30.869 --> 00:53:37.700
Horthy justified his logic of staying in power,
even when controlled by Germany, thusly “I

00:53:37.700 --> 00:53:40.220
cannot let an usurper sit in this place.

00:53:40.220 --> 00:53:42.760
I have sworn to the country not to forsake
it.

00:53:42.760 --> 00:53:44.380
I am still an admiral.

00:53:44.380 --> 00:53:49.930
The captain cannot leave his sinking ship;
he must remain on the bridge to the end.

00:53:49.930 --> 00:53:52.470
Whom will it serve if Imredy sits here?

00:53:52.470 --> 00:53:54.340
Who will defend the army?

00:53:54.340 --> 00:53:59.710
Who will save the million Magyar lads from
being dragged away to the Russian shambles?

00:53:59.710 --> 00:54:05.060
Who will defend the honorable men and women
in this country who have trusted me blindly?

00:54:05.060 --> 00:54:09.190
Who will defend the Jew or our refugees if
I leave my post?

00:54:09.190 --> 00:54:15.240
I may not be able to defend everything, but
I believe that I can still be of great, very

00:54:15.240 --> 00:54:17.020
great, help to our people.

00:54:17.020 --> 00:54:19.720
I can do more than anyone else.”

00:54:19.720 --> 00:54:24.050
Horthy seemed to have stayed true to these
words and tried to fight the best he could;

00:54:24.050 --> 00:54:28.950
the Hungarian fascists, the Jewish deportations,
and the German control over the country.

00:54:28.950 --> 00:54:34.251
At one point, when Romania withdrew from the
Axis in August of 1944, Horthy seized on the

00:54:34.251 --> 00:54:39.260
opportunity of a weakened Eastern front and
tried to retake control of the Hungarian government

00:54:39.260 --> 00:54:42.850
and also quickly signed an armistice treaty
with the Soviets.

00:54:42.850 --> 00:54:48.080
This brief regaining of control over his country
by Horthy lasted only until October when the

00:54:48.080 --> 00:54:52.970
Nazis, who anticipated this move by Horthy,
imprisoned him with the help of the Hungarian

00:54:52.970 --> 00:54:57.990
fascists and, afterwards, forced him to revert
the armistice treaty with the Svoiets and

00:54:57.990 --> 00:55:00.850
abdicate in favor of the Arrowcross.

00:55:00.850 --> 00:55:06.760
Horthy was then, on October 17, taken to the
western train station in Budapest, along with

00:55:06.760 --> 00:55:11.460
his family, and forced to board a train to
Germany where he would remain a prisoner for

00:55:11.460 --> 00:55:12.660
the rest of the war.

00:55:12.660 --> 00:55:18.609
The train which took Horthy to Germany in
1944 took the same path, in the opposite direction,

00:55:18.609 --> 00:55:23.630
as the train which took Horthy from Vienna
to his home in Kenderes in 1918.

00:55:23.630 --> 00:55:30.580
That October 17 1944 was to be the last time
Horthy would ever see Hungary.

00:55:30.580 --> 00:55:35.840
For even though he survived until 1957 mostly
living in Portugal, he was never allowed to

00:55:35.840 --> 00:55:41.540
return to Hungary because the post war government
established in Hungary viewed him “as the

00:55:41.540 --> 00:55:48.770
incarnation of the evil against which progessive
people everywhere had to fight”.

00:55:48.770 --> 00:55:54.609
Well, that was a long video.

00:55:54.609 --> 00:55:58.869
Don’t forget this video is part of a greater
collaboration called Project Dictator where

00:55:58.869 --> 00:56:04.940
various history YouTubers made videos on various
topics on dictators or on people who had been

00:56:04.940 --> 00:56:08.320
called dictators and shouldn't have etc.

00:56:08.320 --> 00:56:13.040
Basically we went with the most broadest definition
of the word dictator and what kind of a video

00:56:13.040 --> 00:56:14.060
we can make about it.

00:56:14.060 --> 00:56:18.359
So if you want to see any of those videos
click the playlist link in the top right corner

00:56:18.359 --> 00:56:20.740
or the description or the pinned comment.

00:56:20.740 --> 00:56:24.720
Hopefully you enjoyed the really long video
this time around, however, don’t always

00:56:24.720 --> 00:56:25.720
expect this.

00:56:25.720 --> 00:56:28.570
This length of a video was more of an exception
for me.

00:56:28.570 --> 00:56:30.080
Let’s see how it’s going to do.

00:56:30.080 --> 00:56:31.080
Hopefully well.

00:56:31.080 --> 00:56:35.550
Hopefully this video is also monetized because
I spend so much time and money working on

00:56:35.550 --> 00:56:44.340
it, if it’s not monetized, maybe please
